    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d528">

                <pb facs="0740" n="664" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg664"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5331/139: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-06T14:00:00+01:00">April 6, 1935—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 6—9:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6. Department’s telegram No. 3, April 5, 5 p.m. Misleading newspaper accounts
                    referred to in my telegram 5, April 4, 11 a.m.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d528-f1"/>
                    were all based on Havas telegram from Washington. Have carried out Department’s
                    instruction by explaining situation to the Secretary General of Ministry of
                    Foreign Affairs, who will issue suitable statement to press.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d528-f1" n="9" xml:id="d528-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported that the newspapers merely published brief factual
                    accounts of the exclusion of Portugal from benefits from the Belgian treaty.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
